cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use braidpy in your work, please cite it as below."
title: braidpy
abstract: >-
  A Python library for working with braids, from braid theory to the braids
  people make: by hand on a kumihimo disk, a marudai or Ashley's stand, or on
  a braiding or lace machine. It computes with braids as braid words, works
  out their invariants and their normal forms, says how to make them, and
  lays and tightens them in 3D.
authors:
